{
  "meta": {
    "collected": "2026-08-12",
    "source": "Etsy shop pages (etsy.com/shop/<name>), fetched same-origin from a logged-in session; shop names came from the listing cards embedded in Marketplace Insights result pages",
    "why_not_apify": "no Apify budget this round - the three inputs the project's own revenue formula needs (sold_count, shop age, active listing count) are all on the public shop page",
    "formula_reference": "methods/revenue-estimation-method: HUF/month = (total sales / months open) x median actual sale price (USD) x 316.33 x catalogue share of the niche",
    "what_is_here": "the first two inputs only - sales per month and catalogue size. The median actual sale price and the catalogue share are NOT measured per shop in this round, so no HUF figure is computed. sales_per_month is a UNIT COUNT, not revenue.",
    "population": "34 shops. Selection: (a) the 11 shops that ranked with 3+ separate listings across 20 niche queries, (b) the top shops by review count from the same card pool. This is NOT a random sample - it is the visible head of the market, and dead or never-ranked shops are structurally invisible (same limitation as data-collection-pipeline).",
    "caveats": [
      "Sales counts are lifetime totals; sales_per_month is a lifetime average, not current run rate. For a 3-month-old shop these are close, for a 15-year-old shop they are not.",
      "'digital' and 'bundle' flags are inferred from the shop's ranking listing TITLES in our card pool, not from a catalogue sample. A shop can be misclassified if its ranking listing is unrepresentative.",
      "Sales are per ORDER, not per file. A mega-bundle sale is one sale."
    ]
  },

